Title: FUN'S "Easter" Cross-Word Puzzle
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-04-12
Number: 17
Notes: A 12x12 stepped diamond with a Maltese cross over the centre (shown as _, printed "No 17", and the intro calls it "the seventeenth in the series"); the third row is printed with the letters EASTER in black-letter type, and two clues start from its E and R squares (E-29, R-30). The square at the right end of the seventh row holds a small cross ornament and no letter (shown as #). The corner pairs 1-2 (BA) and 33-34 (RE) have no clues. No credit line. Printed intro: "Today being Easter Sunday, FUN'S cross word puzzle, the seventeenth in the series, is given an Easter flavoring. Fill in the small squares with letters spelling words corresponding to the clews and definitions given below. Only one letter is to be placed in each square. The solution to this puzzle will be published in next week's FUN." Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_04_12_88.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_04_19_95.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.


