3-4. It comes before Easter. ~ LENT
5-8. That which fastens. ~ FASTENER
9-10. When compelled. ~ MUST
11-12. A horse mackerel. ~ SCAD
13-14. Loose earth. ~ DIRT
15-16. A poem. ~ EPIC
17-18. To put away. ~ STOW
19-20. In hac salus. ~ IHS
21-22. Events from which time is reckoned. ~ ERAS
23-24. Derived from grapes. ~ UVIC
25-28. Thorough scholars. ~ ERUDITES
29-30. They gather no honey. ~ DRONES
31-32. Enemies. ~ FOES
1-6. Excelling all others. ~ BEST
2-7. Before. ~ ANTE
3-10. Used by a cobbler. ~ LAST
4-11. X X X X X X X. ~ TENS
E-29. In an easterly direction. ~ EASTWARD
R-30. Accepts with approval. ~ RECEIVES
5-25. Great enthusiasm. ~ FURORE
8-28. Found in plant cells. ~ RAPHIS
9-21. A small particle. ~ MITE
12-24. A flat circular plate. ~ DISC
22-31. Breakers at the seashore. ~ SURF
23-32. Indians of the Shoshonean tribe. ~ UTES
26-33. Often found locked. ~ DOOR
27-34. Poison for arrows. ~ INEE



